-- data/queststarts.lua
-- Static quest-start and travel text by route step id: a "Start: ..." line
-- on the quest's step, with the NPC's Wiki page attached for right-click >
-- Wiki. Only text: no movement actions, world overlays, paths or arrival
-- checks (Plugin guidelines: no automatically indicating where players
-- should stand or move). No direct game API.
-- main.lua selects which textual travel references to list using recorded
-- quest, level and lodestone checks (not present castability): teleport
-- spells that pass spellReady, and an unlocked alternative lodestone when
-- the named one is locked.
-- From each quest's infobox start point on runescape.wiki (the article URL
-- after each entry), researched October 2026; not re-verified by this
-- comment cleanup.
-- Where the start is two ways, both are named.
-- travel: how to get there, shown as "Travel: ..." under the Start line: the
-- nearest lodestone or the Wiki's own route (runescape.wiki lodestone and
-- location pages, the Wiki's map coordinates for the distances, read
-- 2026-10-20). Only text: the player picks; "if activated" where a
-- lodestone needs it.
-- Provenance: historical Wiki quest, location and lodestone pages underpin
-- these references. The scratch research files used at the time are not
-- available here; each entry's article URL is the public provenance.
-- ring: a fairy ring code the Wiki itself names for that place (quest,
-- location or code-table pages, 2026-10-20): a curated reference, never a
-- live or straight-line nearest calculation. Shown first once A Fairy Tale II is
-- finished; while it's only started, offered after the lodestone "once the
-- Fairy Godfather lets you in" (that step can't be read). Dream Mentor's
-- ring is left out: it ends in two boat trips and the Lunar Isle lodestone
-- is always there for that quest.
-- Lunar Isle's has none: the wiki's Lunar Isle lodestone article, "automatically
-- activated when the player completes Lunar Diplomacy and cannot be activated
-- otherwise", and Dream Mentor needs Lunar Diplomacy. Menaphos's lodestone
-- opens on starting The Jack of Spades, but the wiki's route from it into
-- Sophanem "requires completion of The Jack of Spades and Contact!".

